From 707c522475e4273ab32f543ccafcef419f795f7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhaosiying12138 <neucszhaopeng2016@163.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 23:43:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 42/42] vega: preserve the destination for masked and invalid
 DPP lanes

processDPP substituted the source's own unpermuted value into every lane
that ROW_MASK/BANK_MASK disabled or whose selected source was invalid
under BOUND_CTRL=0. The ISA suppresses the destination write for those
lanes instead. The compiler's canonical wave reduction depends on the
difference: it pairs a row_shr:N with a row_shl:N into one destination
under complementary bank masks, and the substituted values doubled a
partial sum in 24 of every 32 lanes. A lane-exact software emulation of
the old semantics reproduced the wrong Qwen3.5 q/k L2 norms 4096/4096
bit-exact, and the corrected semantics match the reference identically.

Express the control word as two value-level functions in vop_semantics
-- dppLaneWriteEnabled for the row/bank write gate and dppSourceLane for
the lane selection -- and have processDPP return the written-lane mask
so every DPP caller merges into the destination's prior contents. The
replayed recurrent-operator capsule moves from relative L2 0.44 against
the NVIDIA diagnostic oracle to 0.0041, inside the operator contract.

